Niels van Sluis wrote:

> Hi,
>
> I'm trying to intall a AXPpci 33 motherboard with a 233mhz processor. When I
> turn on the power, the power led lights up, but nothing else happens
> (nothing on the screen etc, no sounds nothing...).
>

It can take a fairly long while before anything is displayed on the screen
depending how easy the Bios emulator can get your video card alive.. (> 10
secs.)

> This is how I installed the computer:
>
> Connected the powersuply (from a 386) on the main power connector (J33).
> Added 2 SIMMs (each 8MB non-parity) in bank 0.
> Added a pci Videocard (s3 virge).
> Connected ide floppy and harddisk.
> and connected Power LED connector and speaker connector.
>

Try to startup the system without the floppy and HD cable attached (most IDE
cables are easily put in the wrong way, no notch) Antoher catch may be the fatc
that some older PC power supplies don't generate a decent 'power-good' signal
(usuallly the orange cable at the end) You can check this with a newer PSU.

>
> What am I doing wrong (also tried other videocards (both isa and pci)?
> Do I also need to use the other DC power connector (+3.3V)?
>

S3 Virge should work, at least I run a similar board with a Virge DX/GX version
1.0 (at least that's what Linux cat /proc/pci says...)

Also check the jumper settings, especially the jumper for 'fail-safe floppy
boot' , the jumpers setting the CPU speed, cache ram size and such.


>
> Thanks,
>
> Niels

Gert

(Gooiland boardje?)

