No, because *I* get nervous and have no faith in my electrical ability! :)
If I blow these 2 transistors, I'll only have 2 left to rob off the spare 
board; I think I've got a source for MJ2500's, but the 11349 seems a 
little more elusive..

A little more prodding with a meter at the bad and a good DECwriter have 
shown that the output of the 2 transistors on the good DW while active 
is 16V, and on the other board, 24V. That's quite a difference!

