> 
> I'm obviously ignorant and uninformed, but why does one need this?
> It seems to me that the only use would be for a platform that has
> Acrobat but not a web browser. Is this correct?

Well, first it can be used to generate indexed HTML documents like
user's guides - this means that you don't have to maintain all the
chapter/section links yourself!

It also allows you to write 1 version of your document and "publish"
it in many formats, either for viewing on-line or for printing.

Finally, a lot of people use it to generate printable versions of
their reports and web pages.  In fact, it can be run from a CGI
script/program to generate documents on-the-fly!

