I
>turn on the power, the power led lights up, but nothing else happens
>(nothing on the screen etc, no sounds nothing...).


>What am I doing wrong (also tried other videocards (both isa and pci)?

Have you tried to hit the <ENTER> key ? Some AXPpci33 boards (those with the
PS/2 mouse connector) came with the SRM console that (as a standard?)
enables the serial output as OPA0: console.  If a prompt appears after
hitting the <ENTER> key, nothing is wrong. you've just have to decide
installing:

- OSF/1 (aka DUNIX, Digital Unix)
- Windows NT
- Linux

please refer to appropriate installing guide.  Maybe you have to switch from
console output to Video ouput. Just enter <HELP> for more info.

>Do I also need to use the other DC power connector (+3.3V)?

Not when using "standard" PCI Cards (i.e. all common Video/Network PCI
cards).

