Scott,

Sorry to say the the Celebris 590, other older Celebris low-profile
boxes, and low-profile Venturis boxes use a unique motherboard+riser
card layout.  As far as I know, the motherboard in your system is the
fastest you'll ever have.  Maybe it can run a faster Socket 5
processor, but that's about it.

Similarly, the later low-profile Celebris, Venturis etc systems in the
bone white (official name is frost white) cases are also quite unique.
They use an ATX-connector power supply and a so-called NLX motherboard
layout.  NLX is promoted by Intel as the next new standard for
low-profile computers.  NLX is a lot of hogwash.  The motherboard must
mate with a riser card.  In other words, there is no standard physical
connector, altho the physical dimensions are comparable.  DEC used at
least a half dozen different NLX motherboards for Socket 7, Pentium
Pro, and Pentium II.  Very little interchangability among them.

... Ben Myers

