It would be easy to trivialise into this kind of 
discussion but it isn't really a straight forward 
as that. 

While it may seem like Sun bashing Digital 
and some sort of Sun has bigger boxes (willies) 
than Digital discussion looking at it at that 
level would be a mistake.

Firstly if I was an HP or IBM protagonist 
I would have an equally easy time of it 
when bashing Digital (well maybe IBM may be 
more difficult). Digital promote the idea 
that GS140's and GS60s some how stack up 
against V series, SP's, Origins, NUMA-Q's and 
E6500's they don't. 

Secondly the whole Digital Alpha/NT Story is 
one of marketing vs reality.

On one hand you have Digital marketing the 
B*LL*CKs out of Alpha/NT as the premier NT 
performance platform which having no collateral 
what so ever in the server space to back 
this up. Note this is not a pro Sun standpoint 
simply an observation that Intel/NT boxes 
have better performance numbers on any of the 
publiclically available benchmarks than Alpha/NT 
boxes. 

SAP/R3	HP Netserver/NT beats an 8400/NT
AIM/NT	IBM Netinfinity beats a 4100/NT
Notes bench	ditto
TPC-C		ditto
TPC-D		no NT/Alpha Numbers

etc etc.

If you want to put it in willy terms. Digital
think they are huge but in reality their monster 
is actually a worm.

regards
Andrew Harrison
Enterprise IT Architect



