I do not really know, because we've only one PWS. A PWS433au with NT (and
only sometimes for small tests OpenVMS)

BUT I heard/read:

*) PWS a do not have enough flash memory to contain both AlphaBIOS and SRM.
	Personally I doubt. And if its true, you might replace AlphaBIOS
	with SRM (as you wrote). And if it doesn't work, you may even replace
	the Flash Chip, because the mother board should IMHO be the same...

*) PWS a does have some busses/devices not supported by dUNIX and/or OpenVMS.
	eg. IDE is still supported only for CD-ROMs (w/o Audio) on OpenVMS
	eg. the disk controller is different on PWS a and au for this reason.
	eg. the PS 4D50T graphic controller in my PWS does not work with VMS.

The PWSau is built of not the cheapest devices on the street. It is built
of devices supported by all three DEC opsys (Alpha NT, Digital UNIX, OpenVMS)
and is therefore (unfortunately) more expensive than the PWS a.

So if the firmware is not the problem, your system disk (controller) might be
it...

>The reason I ask is that I know of a PW433a which could greatly benefit
>from such an identity change and would much rather run Unix than
>MasterBates Crashware...

As I'm a VMS fan, UNIX is only the smaller (but earlier) evil. ;-)
And if UNIX, then LINUX (which as you already read, runs on PWS a)
dUNIX (just like OpenVMS) gives you the license headaches, too...

