worth-it keeps a separate database of of your files-it can very busy
when it tries updating itself as you seem to have obsereved.

Easy remove:
Remove the Find Fast shortcut from your Startup Folder via
Start/Settings/Taskbar/Start Menu Programs/Advanced
Totally remove:
Insert your Office CD-go to Start/Settings/Control Panel/Add Remove
Programs/Office from list/Add-Remove/
It will be in a group called "Office Tools"-uncheck it.
while you're, there you could also remove Office Assistant (The cute
but stupid paperclip guy in Office 97) feature. 


