                            (9MEW)

             Date:      26-27th NOVEMBER 1998
             Location:  CLRC Daresbury Laboratory

I am writing to draw your attention to the forthcoming 1998 Machine
Evaluation Workshop to be held on 26th and 27th November at CLRC Daresbury
Laboratory as part of the EPSRC's Distributed Computing Support
Programme. This Workshop is now established as a leading national event
dedicated to distributed high performance scientific computing. The
principle objective is to encourage close contact between the research
communities from the Mathematics, Chemistry, Physics and Materials
Programmes of EPSRC and the major vendors of PCs and workstations, servers,
software and peripherals.

You are invited to attend this year's workshop which will have a format
similar to that of previous years. About a dozen major vendors will make
30-minute presentations on topics such as hardware, compilers, graphics,
storage, networking etc. In past years the audience has been very
appreciative of the technical content of these talks and we have encouraged
the speakers nominated by the vendors to focus their presentations
accordingly.  Important components of the workshop include the availability
of systems for benchmarking evaluation purposes, plus the exhibition itself.
Vendors are providing Internet access to these systems prior to the event,
and the availability of products on the day will help delegates evaluate the
machines.

Past experience suggests that the workshop has proved invaluable to those in
the process of applying for, or actually procuring, local computing
resources. It provides an excellent opportunity to assess current offerings,
and those likely to be released in the near future.

We hope to make loaned systems provided by the vendors available on the
Internet from the 21st November onwards.  Note also that we will be
producing formal Workshop proceedings, a copy of which will be distributed
free to each delegate.

The provisional programme (see URL below for updates) assumes that we will
start on the morning of the 26th November, and finish around 5 p.m. on the
27th.  In view of the limited time available for the organisation of this
workshop, we would be grateful if you would confirm your attendance before
November 19th, 1998.  Please see the contact details below for further
information, or if you have any queries. The WWW page will contain up to
date information as it arrives and also an on-line registration form:

       http://www.dci.clrc.ac.uk/Activity/DISCO+938

We look forward to hearing from you, and hopefully meeting up at the
workshop.

