Austin,
If your machine came with the Xircom 56k 10/100 card, then you shouldn't
be using the Winmodem driver.  IT IS NOT A WINMODEM THAT YOU HAVE, BUT
AN HONEST-TO-GOD, fully hardware modem.  Also, is the Xircom card in the
interal slot (called UMI slot) or one of the two "external" (to the left
of the keyboard) PCMCIA card slots?

If it is in one of the "external" slots, you need to run Xircom drivers
from the Xircom site.  If it is in the UMI slot, accessed by pulling out
a piece of plastic above the floppy drive, then you need to run DEC
drivers.

To the best of my knowledge, machines are shipped with the CEM56k 10/100
card in the UMI slot, which gives you nice connectors at the back of the
machine, but leaves you at the MERCY of DEC to update the drivers...

-- roy

