There is no nfsshare command.  (Nor exportfs.)  To export a directory,
add it to /etc/exports.  You can either edit the file directly or use
adminstrator tools.

Mountd will update the kernel tables on the next mount request or the
next mount command on the server.  (Mount sends  SIGHUP when it mounts
a new disk so mountd can update the exported file handles.)
