Well, you can also remember to do so...

The Software Licensing pages at http://www.digital.com/software-licensing
tell you pretty much what you need to know.  (This was listed in the "Site
Map" from the Digital home page.

Operating system licenses are tied to the system for which they were
originally purchased, and therefore can't be transferred.

You do need to pay to upgrade a base license version, unless you have
purchased a software support contract which includes a "right to new
versions" released during the term of the contract.

