Kent Rankin <kentrankin@theatreorgans.com> wrote:

>    They are rather nice X-terminals(a lot faster than my newer NCD
>X-terminals).  I have been told that they are actually VAXen in
>disguise(VAXStation m76's).I also have a copy of the boot image.

The VXT2000 contains a 22-28 MHz VAX SOC processor (CVAX+CFPU on a single
chip, also used in the VAX 4000 VLC), a DEC SGEC ethernet chip, a serial
port (I forget the chip, but as I recall it was not shared with other
VAXstations), and a 2 bit mono framebuffer (X only used 1 bit mode) or an
8 bit accelerated graphics card (SPX).

As far as I know DEC never released any VXT 2000 software other than
the VXT runtime, and I doubt anyone will port a free UNIX.

