   Digital has never offered any TCP/IP capability for the DECServer
200, only for the 300 series and above. In theory a person could write
their own TCP/IP implementation for one, given sufficient time and
technical information. The possibility was discussed on this newsgroup
a year or so ago, but AFAIK nobody has produced such an implementation.

   Meridian Technology (www.meridian.com) sells a LAT gateway product
which runs under Windows NT and translates between LAT and TCP/IP or
NETBIOS. This presumably could be used to allow a DECServer 200 to
talk to a Linux host. I've never used this product so I can't comment
on how well it works.

