Phillip Helbig wrote in message
<72n2a4$eon$1@probity.mcc.ac.uk>...
>I want to use a VT320 as a console on a VAXstation.  The
VT320 has both
>25 pin and phone plug (DEC423?) connectors.  The
VAXstations have phone
>plugs for the serial connections.  I have the proper
cables.
>
>I seem to remember mention of switches on the back of the
>VAXstation---none on my models (VAXstation 4000/60,
VAXstation 3100 M38
>and VAXstation 3100 M30) have them.
>
On the VAXstation 4000/90 the console switch is on the
front, hidden behind a small panel on the lower right side,
along with the reset switch and status LEDs.  AFAIK the
4000/60 is nearly identical except for CPU speed with the
/90, so I assume the switch would be in the same place.  Try
switching it from the boot prompt too:
>>> SET  console  serial
which also gets rid of those pesky keyboard not plugged in
messages.  Set the VT320 to 9600 baud, 8 bit, no parity, and
use the MMJ jack on the VT320 (RS-423 port).  Make sure the
MMJ plugs are reversed between the VT320 and the 4000 (i.e
you do not have the same color wires next to the MMJ tabs on
both ends of the console cable).  If you are using a
straight thru MMJ cable it won't work.
       Jack Peacock




