In article <72c0e1$5u8$1@news.usit.net>, "Kent Rankin" <kentrankin@theatreorgans.com> writes:
>     I'm not sure, as I don't have the machine at this location, but the
> connector is the DB-style one with the three coax-type connectors in it.
> I'll try and get someone to run the show conf bit, too.

*Most* likely answer then is the 66Hz high-res LCG option.  Under SHOW CONF
this will show up under device 2 with a DEVNAM of LCG and a further line
with HR - 8PLN somewhere on it.

>     What monitors could possibly run on it?

The spec is 1280x1024 fixed resolution at a fixed vertical frequency of 66Hz.
Suitable DEC monitors are VRT16s and VRT19s, either -DA or -HA variants.
Otherwise, any modern multisync monitor which can cope with sync-on-green
RGB input at that spec.

Hardest part may well be finding a suitable cable...

