Well, then we have different option catalogs. My copy of the DPW SOC (V3.7 of
June 19, 1998) states that au-series an add-on Qlogic SCSI controller, with
all systems with serial number 810xxxx or above supporting two of these. There
is no mention of an on-board Qlogic adapter whatsoever in V3.7.

The V2.7 DPW SOC of October 26, 1998 (yes, it is somehow V2.7 - this is not a 
typo) mentions the on-board Qlogic controller and states that two additional
KZPBA's are supported. It makes no reference to the limitations of the older
DPWs, which IMO is very unhelpful. (I have sixteen of pre-810xxxx DPWs around,
and making upgrade and support decisions for them using the V2.7 SOC would be
disastrous).

