We are in need for the part 2T-H7085-GU. We can't get it here in The
Netherlands.
Can anybody help us out!






Here is the problem explaination SUMMARY OF THE PROBLEM KNOWN TO DATE :

As we have determined MasterConsole will emulate the first keyboard it
recognizes when prompted by the operating system. Believe it or not UNIX
questions what keyboard is attached by first asking if it's a OVMS style
keyboard and MasterConsole responds by emulating it because it's the first
asked keyboard type.  

Digital/CSS, Raritan and the UNIX Group worked together to determine if it
would warrant writing a patch or making a change to a future version of
UNIX so the operating system would ask first if a UNIX style keyboard is
attached. UNIX determined that it would create other risks to change the
operating system and the problem is non-existent if no switch is attached
to the systems. UNIX, CSS and Raritan agree there would be less inpact if
Raritans firmware could be changed to exclude OVMS firmware.   
 
Raritan cannot remove the firmware from the switch.



SOLUTION:
-----------------
By chance would there be a Master Console multiple-port switch, Option
2T-H7085-xx installed between the keyboard and the system. There is a KNOWN
issue where the RARITAN Master Console responds to the OS request for
keyboard type with LK411. The fix is a new version of an option call the
"Guardian".

This new "Guardian", part number 2T-H7085-GU is required on ALL Conpaq
Digital UNIX configurations using a RATITAN Master Console Switch.





