The kernel configs differ, but you should be able to build a kernel that
works on both systems, since
the serial controller etc. (which cause problems, between say, the
5000/200 and 5000/240, see a recent
post of mine to this group).
For the 5000/125, the cpu line in the kernel config file is something
like:
cpu "DS5000_100"
Simply add a line
cpu "DSR4_5000_100"
and rebuild the kernel, and this should work on both.
As regards the graphics cards, if they are both recognized as fb's (see
the system startup
messages, uerf -R -r 300), you're in business.

