------

Classic cable and termination problems.

Check that the bus is terminated ONLY at its end.

Check that your Cables are good quality and are not excessively long.
The SCSI spec says about 5 metres ... but that can be too long and
remember that every header type connector you go past adds about 1/3
of a metre and every centronics style connector adds about 2/3 of a
metre.  It you're using external round cables, make sure they are good
and fat ... they must be lot fatter than a power cable ... close to the
diameter of your thumb.

The best rule for SCSI cable length I've heard is that no cable is best!

Cable problems and termination problems are always intensified with more
drives and more activity.

Stuart



