Hi Colin,

Your error indicates the flash rom in cpu's 8 and 9 aren't the same as the
flash rom in cpu 0.
    FLASH FRRC, CPU 8 does not match CPU 0
                 ^ ^ ^ ^
    Flash Rom Recovery Code

Possible causes are:
1) the last cpu module (containing cpu's 8 and 9) isn't the same level as the
other cpu's.
2) the flash rom in the last cpu module is damaged or corrupted.
3) a hardware problem exists in the last slot (these things are very easy to
damage).
4) the level of firmware you're using has a problem with a 10 cpu system.

Trouble shooting suggestions:
1) contact Digital/Compaq and have a qualified CE resolve your problem.
2) exchange the last cpu module with a cpu module in a different slot (not the
first slot) and see if the problem moves with the cpu module
  a) if the problem stays with the slot, try another version of the firmware
and hope the slot isn't damaged.
  b) if the problem stays with the cpu module, try updating it again. If that
doesn't work, return it for repair.

X) I assume all cpu modules are of the same or compatable hardware revision, if
not resolve that problem first.

There are few other, very unlikely, possiblities. The first cpu module is
damaged and isn't communication with the last
cpu module correctly. A power supply module is not functioning correctly (or
you don't have the correct number of power
supply modules for the load).

I believe my first troubleshooting suggestion is the best. Digital/Compaq field
service has the training, equipment and
support services to fix your problem quickly.

Good Luck  Steve Jepsen

