In article <714l3q$f2u$1@nnrp1.dejanews.com>, rceci@adams.com writes:
>> :votes=1
>> :expected_votes=2
>> :disk_quorum="$1$DUA100"
>> :qdskvotes=1
>>
> 
> Ok, I goofed on expected_votes.   (3+1)/2 = 2.  Yes we need 3, not 2.

You set EXPECTED_VOTES to the total votes you ever expect to have booted
into the cluster - in this case 3.  No quorum calculations involved.

However, I'm not sure I agree with Hoff's dire pronouncement concerning your
disk data being at risk, for quorum is still two even with EXPECTED_VOTES=2 .

The quorum scheme is (expected+1)/2, _but you must round up_ .

Also, EXPECTED_VOTES is dynamic and will normally equal the maximum votes
ever seen in the cluster unless you took specific action to reduce it using
the REMOVE_NODE shutdown option or DCL command $ SET CLUSTER/EXPECTED_VOTES .

--
