Dual processor VAX (the VAX 8250 was the single processor version). Followup
to the VAX 8200/VAX 8300. Performance somewhere between 1.2 and 2.3 VUPs
depending on application ( a MicroVAX II was about 0.9 VUPs, A MicroVAX
3100-10 was about 2.4 VUPs ) so somewhat slow by today's standards. Supported
by OpenVMS and ULTRIX and possibly NetBSD. Up to 128MB or memory. VAXBI bus.
Single phase power (at least the UK config is, I expect all are) and eats about
2kW. I guess he already knows the size :-)

