Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

Nope!
 All the original CPU's are at console level 5.1-30. To UPGRADE OR
DOWNGRADE a cpu on 8400's means removing ALL cpu's and installing the new
CPU in TLSB slot 0 ( the primary slot). The new CPU was at rev 5.2-7.  The
LFU is then run, booting from the V5.1 CD and confirmed as rev 5.1-30, with
only this one dual CPU card in the machine. The eeprom is formatted and
built. I then confirm the console level again by initialising.  When the
other CPU's are reinstalled I get the message. Rechecks by placing each CPU
module into slot 0, confirms that they are all at 5.1-30.

Thanks for looking at this anyway..

Colin.

