rouse@my-dejanews.com wrote:
> 
> I have a MSCP driver that talks to a SCSI SQ739 Dilog controller that has a
> Zip unit attached. I'm trying to fix a bug in the driver where by it will
> alert the user if some tries to read/write to Zip unit if there is no disk in
> the drive. I've added a function that will get the unit status of the zip
> drive. However, every time I post the "get unit status" to the controller, it
> hang the machine and I have to reboot to get control again. This only occurs
> is there is no disk in the drive. If there is a disk in the drive, the "get
> unit status" command works fine and does not hang the machine. Does anyone
> have any ideas what I maybe doing wrong here???

I don't think you're doing anything wrong; the problem is that
the firmware on your SQ739 doesn't know how to deal with
your particular removable-media drive.  Contact Dilog and
see if they have a firmware upgrade, or dump the SQ739 and
get a Q-bus host adapter that does deal with Zip drives.  I
know for a fact that CMD and Andromeda controllers do fine
with Zip drives with their latest firmware revisions.

