Subject: Re: Problems running large jobs on an Alpha Workstation (solved)
Date: 1998/11/03
Message-ID: <71mnp1$2ve$1@pisanino.unipi.it>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 407855194
Distribution: world
References: <71g05i$mev$1@pisanino.unipi.it> <ALDERSON.98Nov1182301@netcom.netcom.com>
To: alderson@netcom.com
Organization: Dipartimento di Ingegneria dell'Informazione
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

>> We had the same problem with a Fortran 77 program last summer, after moving to
>> 4.0D on a 533MHz Alpha from OSF/1 1.3a on a 150MHz Alpha.  It's a *user* level
>> problem, solved by setting the appropriate ulimit:

>> >cat /etc/csh.login
>> limit datasize 1048576 kbytes
>> >cat /etc/profile
>> ulimit -d 1048576


Thank you very much, this solved our problem. Now the code is running fine.

