Hi.

I just received my brand new IBM DeskStar 10.1 GB IDE hard drive
today, and I am trying to install it in my Digital Celebris GL 6200
(also called PC 5400) to replace the original Quantum 2.1 GB IDE disk.

Whatever I do I just get "Hard disk failure drive 0" or "...drive 1"
depending on wether I install it as a master or slave. IBM Disk
Manager can see and format the disk, but the PC BIOS won't detect. I'm
able to enter the specs manually (19589/16/63), but I still get the
error message. At one point I got the computer to recognize it as a
8.4 GB disk, but that disappeared when I rebooted.

I found a document on Digital's web site that suggests I enter
1024/16/63 (528 mb) and let the Disk Manager translate, but the BIOS
still won't recognize anything. Just the same old "Hard disk failure
drive 0/1"...

I called Digital Support in Norway, and they tell me that this
computer probably can't take disks larger than 3.2 GB, but I find that
hard to believe... Why can't they write a BIOS version that hooks
int13 to solve the problem? The latest BIOS (v1.08) didn't do anything
good...

Has anyone seen this problem, and does anyone know how to fix it? If I
can't get it to work, I'll have to replace it with a SCSI adapter and
disk to avoid the problem altogether. I need the extra space.

All help appreciated.

Regards,
