In article <363FCFD8.4DE1@mint.net>, Vinal  <museum@mailhost.mint.net> wrote:
>Can someone say the approx value of a PDP 11/03??

That depends on who's buying from whom and under what circumstances.
Commercially, the only real value is for parts to keep old machines
running where replacing the system with something more modern is going
to be expensive, typically where the computer is only a small but
crucial part of an overall system.  To someone with a stalled production
line a vital part may be worth quite a lot of money, but in practice this
doesn;t happen often and the chances of them turning to you if it did
are close to nil unless you're a recognised expert or broker.

But overall, the value for a 11/03, assuming a configuration not too 
far from how it was supplied, is basically the scrap value of the machine,
tens of dollars (US), perhaps a little more parted out.  Talk to a broker;
there's a few out there on the web.

If some looney 8-) offers you $100 for it and brings their own transport, 
take it.

