In article <71g05i$mev$1@pisanino.unipi.it> nodump@voltaire.iet.unipi.it
(Massimo Macucci) writes:

>1594:str2: /sbin/loader: Fatal Error: set_program_attributes failed to set
>heap start

We had the same problem with a Fortran 77 program last summer, after moving to
4.0D on a 533MHz Alpha from OSF/1 1.3a on a 150MHz Alpha.  It's a *user* level
problem, solved by setting the appropriate ulimit:

>cat /etc/csh.login
limit datasize 1048576 kbytes
>cat /etc/profile
ulimit -d 1048576

Of course, you can have each user put this into the appropriate .cshrc or
.profile (for C Shell or Bourne/Korn shells, respectively), but doing it for
all users is so much nicer.
