Thomas,

Probably get flamed for this, but if you have an old Sparc box lying
around, try connecting up and running Sun's format command on the drive
- a little less arcane than the Digital offering and will tell you
immediately if the drive is good. Although the disklabel format won't be
the same, you can also try formatting the drive, doing the bad blocking
and test labelling etc.

Failing that, any PC with an Adaptec controller, whatever, will tell you
if the drive is doa.

I use an old Sun 3 regularly here to test scsi drives etc...

